# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, in the index *and* in the working tree.
#
# Every tracked text file is normalised to LF on commit and checked out as LF on every
# platform. Without this, a Windows checkout produces CRLF working-tree bytes while git
# stores LF, so any hash or byte comparison computed over a tracked text file differs
# between a local run and the Linux CI checkout - a failure that only ever reproduces in
# CI. This repository hashes and diffs tracked text (EULA.md, the submission dossier, the
# generated PBIP project, JSON manifests), so the policy is global rather than per-suffix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be inspected or translated. `text=auto` would detect these
# anyway; declaring them is explicit and cheap.
*.png binary
*.pbiviz binary
*.pbix binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# The embedded custom-visual payload under samples/ is a machine-generated single-line JSON
# document containing the built bundle. It is written byte-for-byte by
# scripts/build-sample-report.mjs and diffed by the submission audit, so it is excluded
# from any conversion at all.
samples/**/CustomVisuals/** -text
